<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is Education Accounting?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>Specialized financial management of schools, colleges, and universities operating as trusts, societies, or Section 8 companies. Covers fee collection tracking, grant accounting, trust fund management, Section 12A tax exemption compliance, and statutory audit under Income Tax Act.</p>
                    <p>For Gurugram schools &ndash; CBSE in DLF, IB on Golf Course Road, university on Sohna Road &ndash; accounting must segregate fee income by type, maintain donation registers per S80G, track capex against corpus, and produce financials satisfying both Haryana Education Department and Income Tax S12A standards. For <a href="/ngo-registration">NGO Registration</a>, see our page.</p>
                    <p>The distinction between exempt educational income and taxable ancillary income (cafeteria, merchandise, commercial rental) requires careful CA oversight. For <a href="/statutory-audit">Statutory Audit</a>, see our page.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Education Accounting:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Section 12A/12AB:</strong> Tax exemption registration for education trusts &ndash; 5-year renewal</li>
                        <li><strong>Form 10B/10BB:</strong> CA audit report filed with ITR-7 by 31 October</li>
                        <li><strong>85% Rule:</strong> Must apply 85% of income for education to keep exemption</li>
                        <li><strong>Notification 12/2017:</strong> GST exemption for pre-school to higher secondary education</li>
                        <li><strong>Haryana Education Rules 2003:</strong> Fee regulation, PTA disclosure, hike limits</li>
                        <li><strong>ITR-7:</strong> Return form for trusts/societies &ndash; due 31 October</li>
                    </ul>

